      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing and drooping on lower leaves often suggests overwatering, as the roots can become stressed and unable to absorb nutrients effectively. Check the soil moisture by sticking your finger a couple of inches down; if it feels soggy, let it dry out more between waterings. Alternatively, if the base of the plant is dry and the leaves are yellowing uniformly, it might need a balanced fertilizer during the growing season.",
