      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the soil is dry and the plant looks drained, consider if the lighting is insufficient; Monsteras thrive with bright, indirect light and can look sickly in low light. Underwatering, despite your care, can sometimes manifest this way, so ensure the pot has adequate drainage to prevent root issues. Also, check the undersides of the leaves for any signs of pests, as even a small infestation can gradually drain a plant's energy.",
